<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xiongnu Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Xiongnu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Xiongnu Empire was a confederation of nomadic peoples that dominated the eastern Eurasian steppe from the late third century BCE to the first century CE. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanyu">chanyu</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modu-chanyu">Modu</a> it united the steppe tribes and became a formidable rival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>, extracting tribute through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heqin">heqin</a> system. Weakened by Han campaigns and internal division, it fragmented, though its political model influenced later steppe empires.</p></div>
